/P 314 0 R
/E (Certificate validation is a critical process in various domains, including education, finance, healthcare, and cybersecurity, where the authenticity and integrity of digital or physical certificates must be verified. Traditional methods of certificate validation often rely on manual checks, centralized databases, or cryptographic techniques, which can be time-consuming, prone to human error, or vulnerable to fraud. With the advent of Artificial Intelligence \(AI\), certificate validation has become more efficient, accurate, and scalable. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
457 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
